      "start": -720,
      "details": "<p>The name Erra-mu\u0161amqit-ayy\u0101b\u012b appears in Akkadian inscriptions of the Neo-Assyrian king Sennacherib dated to 697-695 and 691 B.C. The Nergal gate is called Erra-\u0161\u0101gi\u0161-z\u0101m\u00e2n\u012bya in a text written in 694 B.C.</p>",
      "review_state": "published",
      "description": "Akkadian ceremonial name of the gate, which means \"The God Erra Is the One Who Cuts Down Enemies.\"",
