      "details": "<p>The name Erra-\u0161\u0101gi\u0161-z\u0101m\u00e2n\u012bya appears in and Akkadian inscription of the Neo-Assyrian king Sennacherib dated to 694 B.C. In texts dated to 697-695 and 691 B.C., the \u00a0Nergal gate is called Erra-mu\u0161amqit-ayy\u0101b\u012b.</p>",
